# Phase 6, the two hard signs as the real commands count them: accept fails
# the same check three times, and the result is sent back three times. The
# lead agent is told at once, the person ten minutes later, and the item
# goes when the work is accepted.
agent T1.1: write-result | report done "the page is in" | hang
file brief.md: Target: the shop | Change: your part | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own files | Acceptance: the check passes
orch: init
orch: run new "the shop"                            -> expect r1
task T1 "The page" --name page --check "test -f page.txt" --brief brief.md
orch: start T1                                      -> expect "(T1.1)"
await: attempts T1.1 reported
orch: accept T1                                     -> expect exit 1
orch: accept T1                                     -> expect exit 1
orch: accept T1                                     -> expect exit 1
orch: reject T1 "page.txt is not there"
orch: status --sweep --quiet
orch: wait --timeout 0                              -> expect stuck T1 "the same check failed 3 times"
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 0
as-worker T1.1: report done "the page is in now"
orch: reject T1 "still no page.txt"
as-worker T1.1: report done "the page is in, really"
orch: reject T1 "and still none"
orch: status --sweep --quiet
term-event working T1
clock +11m
orch: status --sweep --quiet
human: status --items --json                        -> expect n1 "page looks stuck" "the same check failed 3 times · sent back 3 times" "The lead agent was told"
file page.txt: the page
as-worker T1.1: report done "the page is there"
orch: accept T1                                     -> expect "T1 is done, checked"
orch: status --sweep --quiet
assert: T1 status done; n1 state closed; no event lost; no event twice
